  "intro": "In the present Arabic needs no 'is': الْجَوُّ لَطِيف (the weather is pleasant). To describe the past, add كَانَ (was), or كَانَتْ for a feminine subject, and give the describing word the -an ending: كَانَ الْجَوُّ لَطِيفًا (the weather was pleasant). For 'I was' and 'we were' the stem shortens: كُنْتُ, كُنَّا.",
  "objectives": [
    "Describe a past holiday with كَانَ and كَانَتْ",
    "Add the -an ending to a description after كَانَ",
    "Say where you travelled and how long you spent there",
    "Pronounce the emphatic ṣ and ṭ in الصَّيْف and بِالطَّائِرَة"
